[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Starlark for .NET - quality, tooling and delivery
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Draft, Active, Implemented, Open)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False

[FREETEXT]
How the project is tested, measured, documented and shipped.
[/FREETEXT]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Testing

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Unit and conformance tests
STATEMENT: >>>
The repository shall contain xunit tests for the syntax and evaluation layers and the official conformance data, and
all shall pass.
<<<
VERIFICATION: dotnet test

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Example programs as tests
STATEMENT: >>>
There shall be at least 50 example Starlark programs that state their expected output or error in comments and are
executed by one parameterized test.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests.ThereAreFiftyOrMoreExamples

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-008
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Sample applications as tests
STATEMENT: >>>
Each sample application (Adventure, BuildRules, ConfigInspector, GameAI, Mandelbrot, ParallelBuilds, PolicyEngine, RayTracer,
ReportPipeline) shall be run by a test that asserts on its key output, and the Level II BASIC interpreter written in
Starlark shall be tested for its statements, DATA/READ, the EDIT command, non-ASCII text and the SIN demonstration program.
<<<
VERIFICATION: AppTests, ExamplesTests, BasicTests, BasicExprTests, BasicDataTests, BasicEditTests, BasicNonAsciiTests, BasicSineTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Fuzzing
STATEMENT: >>>
Seeded fuzzers shall exercise the lexer, parser, interpreter and checker, with iteration count and seed settable by
environment variable.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Fuzz.Tests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Property tests
STATEMENT: >>>
Hedgehog property tests with shrinking shall check invariants of the parser, interpreter and checker.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Fuzz.Tests (PropertyTests)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: FsCheck properties
STATEMENT: >>>
FsCheck properties shall complement the Hedgehog ones for the value model and the host interop conversions.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Fuzz.Tests (InteropProperties)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Mutation testing
STATEMENT: >>>
Stryker.NET shall run against Starlark.Eval and Starlark.Syntax with the configuration in stryker-config.json, and the
build shall fail below the break threshold.
<<<
VERIFICATION: stryker-config.json; tools/MutantReport; OpsMutationTests, MethodsMutationTests
COMMENT: Ops.cs went 73.5% to 93.7% and Methods.cs 79.2% to 84.8% after adding survivor tests. Values, StringFormat, Json, Interpreter, the checker, Ty and Interop are not yet run.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-ROB-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: No crash on any input
STATEMENT: >>>
No input shall make the lexer, parser, checker, interpreter or host interface crash, hang, or consume unbounded memory or
disk. Malformed, truncated, hostile and oversized input shall end in a bounded, reported error. Every component that reads
user input shall have error-path and truncation tests, an exhaustive test over all short strings of a small alphabet where
the input has a grammar, and a guard that fails fast if a loop over input stops making progress.
<<<
VERIFICATION: LexerRegressionTests (exhaustive short inputs, progress guard); ExhaustiveInputTests; StackDepthTests; ReleaseCandidate1Tests (review findings: cyclic and deep host conversion, int size cap, bounded strings, futures limits) (deep and cyclic values); BoundedExpansionTests; NestingLimitTests (Go's 1000-level nesting limit on every parser path, the parser call-graph check, 200,000 nested ifs); GoLimitsTests (the deepest allowed program on a 1 MB stack, long operator chains, Go's repetition and shift limits, a big script stack and 100,000-deep recursion); Starlark.Fuzz.Tests (DeepNestingNeverCrashes); tools/Soak with child memory cap and disk floor
COMMENT: Added after an unterminated f-string format spec (f'{:) made the lexer loop and exhaust memory during a soak run. Extended on 2026-11-06 after deeply nested source text (1000 nested lists, unary operators or `not`, or a 1000-term sum) crashed the process with a stack overflow; the limits adopted from Starlark-Go are listed in docs/DEVIATIONS.md.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-TST-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fourteen-hour soak
STATEMENT: >>>
A C# soak tool shall run the fuzzers and property tests in a loop for a configurable duration (default 14 hours), with
a fresh seed per round, a wall-clock limit per input, failing inputs written to disk, periodic progress and memory
logging, and the ability to resume.
<<<
VERIFICATION: tools/Soak; a first 5-hour run found 116 failing rounds and 6 hangs, all fixed (BoundedExpansionTests)
COMMENT: Part A of an 18-hour run (three 6-hour parts with a fix pass between) is queued; mark Implemented when the run completes clean.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Coverage

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-COV-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Coverage report
STATEMENT: >>>
A C# tool shall merge Cobertura reports from all test projects and write Markdown and HTML summaries with per-file
uncovered lines.
<<<
VERIFICATION: tools/CoverageReport

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-COV-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Coverage targets
STATEMENT: >>>
Total line coverage shall be at least 96 percent, and Methods.cs, Values.cs and StringFormat.cs at least 95 percent each.
<<<
COMMENT: Currently 94.4 percent lines and 88.1 percent branches.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Performance

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-PERF-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Own benchmark
STATEMENT: >>>
A benchmark project shall measure lexer, parser and interpreter throughput.
<<<
VERIFICATION: bench/Starlark.Bench

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-PERF-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Comparison with the Rust implementation
STATEMENT: >>>
Lexer and parser speed shall be compared with starlark-rust on the same inputs and the result recorded.
<<<
COMMENT: Needs a Rust toolchain, which is not installed.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Documentation and packaging

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-DOC-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Deviations
STATEMENT: >>>
Deliberate deviations from the specification and from the reference implementations, and the embedding limits, shall
be recorded in docs/DEVIATIONS.md.
<<<
VERIFICATION: docs/DEVIATIONS.md

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-DOC-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Embedding guide and example applications
STATEMENT: >>>
There shall be an embedding guide and runnable example applications that show host functions, object exposure, loading,
limits, type checking and error reporting, with automated tests.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ManualTests (every code sample in docs/MANUAL.md and README.md is run), AppTests
COMMENT: The guide is docs/MANUAL.md; docs/site/deep-dive.html explains the implementation with live examples, checked in a headless browser by tools/BuildSite --check.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-DOC-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Requirements traceability
STATEMENT: >>>
Every Implemented requirement shall name a verifying test, and a check shall fail the build when a named test does not
exist.
<<<
VERIFICATION: tools/Trace (exit code 1 when an Implemented requirement names no existing test)
COMMENT: Trace is a tool run by hand, not yet part of a build: wiring it into CI belongs to QA-PKG-002.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-PKG-001
STATUS: Open
TITLE: NuGet packages
STATEMENT: >>>
Starlark.Syntax and Starlark.Eval shall build as NuGet packages with metadata, XML documentation and a README.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-PKG-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Continuous integration
STATEMENT: >>>
A CI workflow shall build, test with coverage, enforce the coverage threshold and run mutation tests on a schedule.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Project conventions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: QA-CON-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Language and tooling
STATEMENT: >>>
Helper programs shall be written in C#. Requirements shall be kept in StrictDoc. Code comments shall be XML
documentation comments. Property testing shall use Hedgehog and FsCheck, and mutation testing Stryker.NET.
<<<
COMMENT: The test runner stays xunit by the owner's decision.

[/SECTION]
